  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "17. Monsters And Vehicles",
    "ruleNumber": "17.02",
    "summary": "Models without bases have FRAME, as do certain other large models. This modifies Measuring Distances. For a position measured to or from a FRAME model, use the nearest point on the model itself, even if it has a base. Follow any measurement point specified by the rule. A FRAME model without a base may turn freely around its central axis during a move, provided it stays upright.",
